    "rulings": [
      {
        "answer": "Yes, you can.  Even if you only reveal one of the applicable cards, you can still add it to your hand.",
        "question": "If the 3 cards revealed for this card's [On Play] effect include only either 1 card with [Avian] or [Bird] in any of its traits or 1 card with the [Vortex Warriors] or [LIBERATOR] trait, can I just add that 1 card to my hand?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "No, you can't.  If you have cards that are targets of this effect, you must add as many cards to your hand as possible.",
        "question": "If the 3 cards I reveal from my deck for this card's [On Play] effect include both a card with [Avian] or [Bird] in any of its traits and a card with the [Vortex Warriors] or [LIBERATOR] trait, can I choose to only add one of them to my hand, and place the remaining cards at the bottom of my deck?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      }
